cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Skyline fMRI in your research, please cite it, together with the
  DIPY and FURY papers listed under references.
title: "Skyline fMRI: functional, structural and diffusion MRI visualization"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Atharva
repository-code: "https://github.com/Atharva-Shah-2298/skyline-fmri"
url: "https://github.com/Atharva-Shah-2298/skyline-fmri"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
abstract: >-
  Skyline fMRI is an interactive, GPU-accelerated viewer that shows BOLD runs,
  thresholded activation maps, anatomy, diffusion maps and tractography in one
  scene. It plays BOLD time series, fits task GLMs and seed correlations,
  links white-matter tracts to activation clusters, renders glass brains and
  triplanar views, and exports figures at print resolution on white, black or
  transparent backgrounds.
keywords:
  - fMRI
  - diffusion MRI
  - tractography
  - glass brain
  - visualization
  - neuroimaging
references:
  - type: article
    title: "DIPY, a library for the analysis of diffusion MRI data"
    authors:
      - family-names: Garyfallidis
        given-names: Eleftherios
      - name: "et al."
    journal: "Frontiers in Neuroinformatics"
    volume: 8
    start: 8
    year: 2014
    doi: "10.3389/fninf.2014.00008"
  - type: article
    title: "FURY: advanced scientific visualization"
    authors:
      - family-names: Garyfallidis
        given-names: Eleftherios
      - name: "et al."
    journal: "Journal of Open Source Software"
